  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: AppPhys 4
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "You\u2019ve been tracking how your patients do on a new, recently approved
    treatment compared to standard options so you can share what you learn with your
    cancer center\u2019s treatment committee.\n\n<b>In this scenario, what is the
    physician\u2019s role in post-market research once a new treatment is approved?</b>"
  explanation: "Even after approval, physicians play a key role in evaluating how
    new treatments work in real-world care alongside existing options, ensuring they\u2019re
    used in the right ways and for the right patients. By closely tracking outcomes,
    side effects, and patient experiences, they help identify when a treatment is
    truly beneficial or when another option may be better. This real-world feedback
    helps refine treatment guidelines and improves care for future patients."
  correctAnswer: Physicians continue to evaluate how the new treatment performs compared
    to standard options, helping refine when and for whom they should be used.
  incorrectAnswer1: Only the physician(s) on the research team decide how it fits
    into care.
  incorrectAnswer2: Physicians should prescribe it to all their patients as a treatment
    alternative to the other standard therapies.
  incorrectAnswer3: None of these answers
  questionRole: Physician
  questionType: MultipleChoice
  questionStage: Approval
